/*
 * Implicit cast validation.
 *
 * CastImplicitValidation performs semantic validation of implicit casts
 * between values and types. It is responsible for:
 *
 *   - verifying type compatibility,
 *   - reducing values through compile-time interpretation,
 *   - recursively validating implicit casts inside blocks, lazy values,
 *     futures, and enum field accesses,
 *   - delegating scalar and compound implicit casts to specialized modules,
 *   - producing rewritten values when implicit casts succeed,
 *   - propagating detailed diagnostics when implicit casts fail.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::validator::value::operator::cast_::implicit
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/validator/value/operator/cast_/implicit.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-06-14
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
